    "created_at": "2020-05-20T23:35:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-05-20T23:35:33Z",
    "body": "Well, imho, before we can finally go to `v1.0.0` release, we should at least address the long waiting time in `git_status`. It seems a bad choice to me if users still have to wait a long time in a large git repo in stable.\r\n\r\nAdding man pages, or config wizards, or optionally packages for different distributions (deb, AUR, etc.) may also be considered before `v1.0.0`.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
